Decide (maintainer). From k347 (choices worker, 2026-10-31): a control plane's `service:` key is written by `ocp init --provider local --service` and read by nothing in lib/, bin/ or share/. Since k347, validate() still accepts it, as one of the keys it lists. Options:
- drop it: init stops writing it, and validate() refuses it with a hint;
- keep it as a placeholder (say what for);
- make it mean something (what, with --service).
Not to be built before the maintainer answers.

Maintainer's decision 2026-11-06 (hub perl-developer-bb, kubernetes-ocp-entscheidungen.md, e0ba4b5): the service: key goes. ocp init no longer writes it; validate() refuses it with a hint that it is gone and can be deleted. init's --service option goes with it if it only writes this key.

2026-11-06 ocp-release-1106 (ocp-choices-worker): service: is out of the control-plane keys; validate() refuses it as an unknown key with the hint: service is gone (ocp init wrote it, nothing read it) -- delete it. Untagged like every unknown control-plane key, so apply and keys secure refuse it. --service only validated systemd|none and wrote the key, so it is gone; init --service now fails as an unknown option. write_spec writes no service. New t/357 (5 claims); t/296, t/308, t/41 claims replaced. Red on 8e9956b (claims 1,2,4,5), mutants for 2 and 3; binding 8 files, 216 tests, PASS.

